# Blepharoplasty and/or Repair for Blepharoptosis — IEHP / Medi-Cal Provider Manual (Aug 2020)
library "Blepharoplasty And Blepharoptosis Repair".

/*
COVERED-SERVICE CODE SETS - the RECORD ARM of the two request concepts.

These value sets are authored here and are INTENDED TO SURVIVE INTO PRODUCTION. That is an exception
to the usual convention (an authored value set is normally a placeholder the deployment overwrites)
and it is deliberate - operator ruling. Do not delete them expecting prod to supply a replacement.

The codes are an INFERENCE, not a quotation: the policy never states its covered-service scope, and
these CPT codes appear once, inside a parenthetical about photographs. That inference is load-bearing
because these sets decide which requests DENY, so it is flagged @customer-confirmable for medical
validation to rule on. See the flag store.

SHAPE, and BOTH halves are load-bearing:
  - The `system is` + `code is` lines are what make these sets REAL. A terminology with neither emits
    a STUB value set matching nothing, which would turn "deny when absent" into "deny everything".
  - There is deliberately NO `valueset is` url line. With one present the emitter also emits a `code`
    declaration PER CODE, every one of them named after the TERMINOLOGY rather than the code - so the
    identifier is declared 1+N times and the CQL library never compiles. Downstream, `$populate`
    evaluates nothing, the request gate never opens, and every questionnaire comes back with only the
    request items and every response empty. Measured 2026-09-04 and reproduced by the CRL team.
    Dropping the line costs nothing: the emitted ValueSet url and id are byte-identical either way
    (both namespaced to `mcpm-bleph-...`), the CPT codes still emit in `compose` and `expansion`, and
    the retrieve references the terminology by NAME in either shape.
*/

terminology "Blepharoplasty Service Codes":
- system is `http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt`.
- code is `15822`.
- code is `15823`.

terminology "Blepharoptosis Repair Service Codes":
- system is `http://www.ama-assn.org/go/cpt`.
- code is `67901`.
- code is `67902`.
- code is `67903`.
- code is `67904`.
- code is `67905`.
- code is `67906`.
- code is `67907`.
- code is `67908`.

/*
SOURCE: Medi-Cal Provider Manual, Part 2 - Surgery: Eye and Ocular Adnexa, page updated August 2020.
PRIOR AUTHORIZATION (TAR). Deployment: IEHP, disposition mode "embedded".

CUSTOMER RULINGS live in the review-flag store (src/medical-validation/flags/) and are CITED, not
restated here - the store is the authority, and a copy in this header could only drift from it.

DISPOSITION SET - 2-way { certify.Met, not-certify.Unmet }. `pended` is permitted by embedded mode
but not authorised by this narrative: mode gates finality, it does not supply a reason the policy
never gives.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
THREE CONJOINED LAYERS, NOT ONE FACT RECORDED THRICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
A qualifying INDICATION and a documented COMPLAINT and an objective DEMONSTRATION. The lists run
near-parallel but do not overlap: the indications carry etiology and "symptomatic"/"chronic"
qualifiers a photograph cannot establish, and the demonstrations carry numeric bars the indications
lack. Merging in either direction drops source content.
  The policy does NOT require the evidence to match the indication. Each list carries its own fresh
  "one or more of the following" - they quantify independently - so a dermatitis indication supported
  by a qualifying visual-field printout passes. Adding correspondence would narrow the written rule.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LEAF DEPTH - THE TEST
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SPLIT when the parts could be ANSWERED DIFFERENTLY and the decision - or the evidence required -
could turn on which one is true. RIDE when the parts are interchangeable for the determination.

The test is CRL-native rather than grammatical: a leaf IS a question on the emitted Questionnaire, so
minting one asks "could a respondent answer these differently, and would anything downstream care?"
"near or far" rides not because it modifies a noun but because nothing branches on it; if a revision
paid differently for near vs far, the same words would split.

Applied here: indication and complaint items naming several separately-reportable findings are split
per finding; "at distance and/or near" and "with upper lid skin and/or lid margin in repose and
elevated" ride, the latter naming WHAT IS REPOSITIONED during the test rather than two findings.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"CONFORMING" IS LOAD-BEARING IN EVERY EVIDENCE CONCEPT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Page 3 opens "Providers MUST CONFORM to the following standards" - prints not slides, frontal
canthus-to-canthus, head perpendicular, clarity sufficient to show the corneal light reflex; Goldmann
III 4-E or an equivalent automated perimeter, 10dB stimulus, 50-60 degrees above fixation, the
tangent-screen alternative. Those standards are MANDATORY and constrain what counts as evidence.

They do not get leaves of their own - they are CONSTITUTIVE of the evidence answer and ride in its
identity, because a respondent holds ONE artifact and answers ONE question about it: is this a
conforming photograph showing X? The test that settles whether that is legitimate rather than a
criterion-drop is: IS THERE ANY BRANCH THAT CAN FAIL ON NON-CONFORMING EVIDENCE? Here yes - a
submission missing the required additional or oblique photographs is non-conforming, the evidence
question is answered no, and the request lands on not-certify.Unmet. Conformance can deny. What it
does not get is a branch of its OWN.

THE TWO CONDITIONAL PAGE-3 BULLETS, read against the source:
  - "If redundant skin coexists with true lid ptosis, additional photos must be taken with the upper
    lid skin retracted" - this is the BOTH-PROCEDURES case, and the next source clause states the
    requirement it serves: "If both a blepharoplasty and a ptosis repair are planned, both must be
    individually documented." That IS encoded, as two per-procedure documentation leaves. The
    retracted-skin photograph is the MECHANISM of individual documentation, not a separate criterion.
  - "Oblique photos are ONLY NEEDED ... WHEN THIS IS THE ONLY INDICATION for surgery" - read the
    modality: a RELAXATION, not a requirement. It says when oblique photographs may be SKIPPED.
    Minting it as a required leaf would ADD a burden the source is removing.
  KNOWN LIMIT, recorded rather than papered over: both are CONDITIONAL on the decision's own facts
  and a static adjective cannot carry them. They govern which images to include, not whether the
  request qualifies - which is why they ride. The third conditional bullet on that page (both
  procedures individually documented) IS broken out, because it does change whether a request
  qualifies.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
STAGE BOUNDARY - VALUE THRESHOLDS AS ASSERTED BOOLEANS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The value thresholds this policy names are ones the kit defers, so they ship as provider-asserted
booleans. Because no engine evaluates the comparison, THE COMPARISON LIVES IN THE QUESTION: each
threshold rides in the concept name and the code.
  "approaches TO WITHIN 2.5 mm of the corneal light reflex" means 2.5 mm OR LESS - a SMALLER
  margin-to-reflex distance is worse ptosis and is what qualifies. Every other threshold here reads
  "a minimum of". Named in the source's own direction so it cannot be inverted.
  The visual-field criterion is NOT "loss in repose and elevated". The source tests the lid in repose
  and again elevated by taping "to demonstrate potential correction by the proposed procedure" - the
  elevation exists to show the improvement is surgically achievable.

NOT ENCODED, deliberately:
  - The ICD-10-CM list. The source says the codes "support medical necessity" and are expressly "not
    required for claim reimbursement", so a required-diagnosis conjunct would ADD a gate the policy
    disclaims.
  - The page-3 technique standards AS CRITERIA - see the CONFORMING note; they ride instead.
  - "in respose" is a source typo for "repose"; corrected in the concept identities, and the anchor
    keeps the source's spelling.

THE PROSTHESIS INDICATION IS ALL BUT UNREACHABLE, and the customer has ruled it correct as encoded.
"Prosthesis difficulties in an anophthalmic socket" has a matching demonstration option, but the
COMPLAINT list - a required conjunct - offers no matching member, so that indication plus its
matching photograph, with no listed complaint, returns not-certify.Unmet. Pinned by a CEL case so the
behaviour stays visible.
*/

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Determinations - NOT declared here. This workspace vendors the shared IEHP determination
// library beside the policy (src/crl/medical-policy-determination.crl), trimmed to EXACTLY the
// two activities this decision recommends, so the disposition vocabulary stays one artifact
// across policies instead of drifting per file. See that file for why not-certify.Cosmetic is
// NOT among them (review flag 21dc988d).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Request gate - TWO separately requestable procedures. Page 3's "if both are planned, both must
// be individually documented" confirms they are ordered and documented separately, so the source's
// "and/or" becomes STRUCTURE in the guard rather than a coordinating conjunction inside one leaf.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// REFACTOR:grounded (#320, review 564): requests are independent positive-witness publications.
// No matching source is unknown, not a negative. Local false/unknown joins source true before final
// recency selection. This fixture explicitly prefers a unique local candidate at equal time.
// Active order requests are supported; other states need explicit eligibility capability.


