// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LAYER 1 - the four medical-necessity indications ("one of the following").
// Indication 1 names THREE etiologies, which are distinct diagnoses a chart records separately.
// "near or far" is the source's own scope on the impairment and rides in each identity.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Customer ruling, flag c7dd860f: the narrative is "Symptomatic redundant skin weighing down upper
// lashes". Name and code are that wording exactly. "Symptomatic" is load-bearing.
/*
These finite coded questions retain one selected answer per concept. An explicit
listed-negative answer makes membership false; missing evidence remains unknown.
The selected Record supplies population and value reads. shape reduction is most
recent chooses among dated alternatives and reports unresolved ties or undated
competition. Prefer-local cannot choose between two local answers.
One answer slot does not preserve multiple coexisting findings; revisit that
model if a downstream use requires the full collection.
*/

/*
THE FUSED INDICATION QUESTION - the source sentence encoded as the ONE question it is:

  "The service is considered medically necessary when performed as FUNCTIONAL/RECONSTRUCTIVE SURGERY
   TO CORRECT ONE OF THE FOLLOWING:"  + four bullets

WHICH listed indication is this surgery performed to correct? One question, one answer.

WHY THE FUSION IS MORE FAITHFUL, not merely smaller:
  1. THE SOURCE STATES ONE REQUIREMENT, not two. No sentence says the patient must HAVE the
     condition; having it is entailed by the surgery correcting it. Encoding "has X" as its own
     criterion asks a question the source never asks.
  2. THE PAIRING IS STRUCTURAL. With an indication side and a purpose side as separate atoms in
     different OR-arms, nothing stopped a submitter affirming one indication and a DIFFERENT
     purpose - the tree accepted the mismatch. One answer cannot be inconsistent with itself.
  3. THE PURPOSE QUALIFIER STOPS HOLLOWING. "functional/reconstructive" now lives in the QUESTION,
     where it governs every option at once and cannot be dropped from one of them.

THE FIRST ITEM KEEPS ITS DECOMPOSITION as one option per etiology-by-finding pairing. Vision
impairment and a visual field defect are separately measured - acuity vs perimetry - and the policy's
own evidence layer keeps them apart ("either a photograph OR the visual field examination printout").
The causal "due to" rides IN each option: modelling finding and etiology as separate answers would
let an unpaired combination qualify, dropping the causal attribution the source requires.

The residual "surgery targets something not on the list" case is the `none of the listed` answer.
*/

concept "Which Listed Indication Is This Functional Or Reconstructive Surgery Performed To Correct":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is CodeableConcept.
- code is `functional-or-reconstructive-surgery-performed-to-correct-indication`.
- value domain is answer options.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- value from:
  - `near-or-far-vision-impairment-due-to-dermatochalasis` display is `Impairment of near or far vision due to dermatochalasis`, qualifying.
  - `near-or-far-vision-impairment-due-to-blepharochalasis` display is `Impairment of near or far vision due to blepharochalasis`, qualifying.
  - `near-or-far-vision-impairment-due-to-blepharoptosis` display is `Impairment of near or far vision due to blepharoptosis`, qualifying.
  - `visual-field-defect-due-to-dermatochalasis` display is `Visual field defect due to dermatochalasis`, qualifying.
  - `visual-field-defect-due-to-blepharochalasis` display is `Visual field defect due to blepharochalasis`, qualifying.
  - `visual-field-defect-due-to-blepharoptosis` display is `Visual field defect due to blepharoptosis`, qualifying.
  - `symptomatic-redundant-skin-weighing-down-upper-lashes` display is `Symptomatic redundant skin weighing down upper lashes`, qualifying.
  - `chronic-symptomatic-dermatitis-of-pretarsal-skin-caused-by-redundant-upper-lid-skin` display is `Chronic, symptomatic dermatitis of pretarsal skin caused by redundant upper lid skin`, qualifying.
  - `prosthesis-difficulties-in-an-anophthalmic-socket` display is `Prosthesis difficulties in an anophthalmic socket`, qualifying.
  - `none-of-the-listed-indications` display is `None of the listed indications`, not qualifying.

