// Selected coded answers preserve the narrative pairing between functional/
// reconstructive purpose and its indication. Unanswered membership stays unknown.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LAYER 3 - the objective demonstration: a CONFORMING photograph OR a CONFORMING visual field.
// What is encoded is the DEMONSTRATED FINDING, never "a photograph was attached" - attachment is
// administrative completeness for the PAS workflow; the finding is substantive.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
concept "Submitted Photographs Conform To The Photograph Submission Standards":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `submitted-photographs-conform-to-the-photograph-submission-standards`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

concept "Submitted Visual Field Examination Conforms To The Visual Field Examination Standards":
- shape is Record.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `submitted-visual-field-examination-conforms-to-the-examination-standards`.
- shape reduction is most recent.

// The comparison is repose-vs-elevated to demonstrate POTENTIAL CORRECTION by the proposed
// procedure - not merely loss measured twice - and it is the upper lid skin and/or lid margin that
// is placed in repose and elevated by taping.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The both-procedures documentation rule - "both must be INDIVIDUALLY documented", so two leaves.
// One opaque yes/no could not say WHICH procedure lacked documentation, and partial documentation
// is a real state the source distinguishes.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
concept "The Requested Blepharoplasty Is Individually Documented":
- shape is Record.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `blepharoplasty-individually-documented`.

concept "The Requested Blepharoptosis Repair Is Individually Documented":
- shape is Record.
- shape reduction is most recent.
- type is Observation.
- value type is boolean.
- code is `blepharoptosis-repair-individually-documented`.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The three layers as named branch guards. Post-#236 a criterion lowers ONCE to a named boolean
// define referenced by identity, so each disjunction is ONE parent DNF leaf while its atoms stay
// visible in the define body and the use-site input[].
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
criterion "Qualifying Functional Indication":
// ONE ANSWER. See the fused-question block above for why this is no longer four OR-arms pairing an
// indication with its purpose. `none of the listed indications` is the determinate denial, and it
// costs one answer where the previous shape cost nine.
- when ( "Qualifying Functional Indication Selected" ).

criterion "Qualifying Patient Complaint Documented":
// The source lists several complaints, any one of which satisfies this - so this is ONE question
// with an answer per listed complaint, not a question per complaint: the coded question "Documented
// Patient Complaint". As separate booleans it cost one "no" per complaint to deny, and PAUSED the
// whole determination if any was left blank (a bare `code is` concept is value-read, so unanswered
// is UNKNOWN, not false). As one question it costs ONE: "None of the listed complaints".
- when ( "Qualifying Patient Complaint Reported" ).

criterion "Qualifying Objective Demonstration Submitted":
// TWO EVIDENCE LANES, each gated by ITS OWN conformance atom conjoined with ITS OWN coded
// demonstration question.
//
// CONFORMANCE IS ITS OWN ATOM, one per lane. The source states the submission standards ONCE PER
// LANE ("Providers must conform to the following standards when submitting photographs"), governing
// the SUBMISSION - not once per finding. Fusing conformance into each evidence leaf as an adjective
// would ask the same conformance question once per finding and leave a submitter no way to say the
// true thing: "the photograph shows skin on the lashes, but it does not meet the standards".
// As its own atom, conformance is separately answerable and separately deniable.
//
// THE FINDINGS ARE A CODED QUESTION PER LANE - photographic, and visual field. As separate booleans
// it cost one "no" per finding to deny this criterion; as a question per lane it costs one per lane.
- when ( ( "Submitted Photographs Conform To The Photograph Submission Standards"
       and "Qualifying Photographic Demonstration Shown" )
      or ( "Submitted Visual Field Examination Conforms To The Visual Field Examination Standards"
       and "Qualifying Visual Field Demonstration Shown" ) ).

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Decision - the leaves enumerated below, over two dispositions, `first:` operative at every level.
//   1. both procedure determinations explicitly false               -> not-certify.Unmet
//      missing request determinations pause before any leaf
//   2. performed for cosmetic purposes                              -> not-certify.Unmet
//   3. BOTH requested, three layers + BOTH individually documented   -> certify.Met
//   4. BOTH requested, otherwise                                     -> not-certify.Unmet
//   5. one requested, three layers                                   -> certify.Met
//   6. one requested, otherwise                                      -> not-certify.Unmet
// The cosmetic branch is hoisted ABOVE the both/one split so it is asked exactly once.
//
// ⚠ LEAF 1 IS A DEPLOYMENT CONVENTION, NOT A POLICY STATEMENT. The source says nothing about
// requests for some other service; in embedded mode this leaf should be unreachable because
// service routing happens upstream. Retained because the kit prescribes nesting the request gate;
// its CEL case pins the structure, not a source rule.
//
// ⚠ MOST LEAVES SHARE A DISPOSITION - every leaf but the Met ones recommends not-certify.Unmet, so
// a CEL `result is` oracle cannot tell them apart: it checks disposition MEMBERSHIP only. Leaf
// coverage is provable; PATH proof is not, and no CEL authoring closes it (`nodeId` is trace-only;
// `viaWhen` is null on every `otherwise`). REPORTED, not authored around - minting flavors to
// sharpen the oracle would corrupt a disposition set the customer has already ruled on.
//   ⚠⚠ THIS GAP IS NOT THEORETICAL, AND IT BIT. The judge pass mutated the tree by ONE LINE -
//   demoting the cosmetic branch below the both-requested branch - and the whole 29-case suite
//   stayed green while a cosmetic both-procedure request started returning certify.Met, which the
//   source forbids outright. The re-encode had DROPPED the case that catches it; the prior
//   encoding carried it. It is restored as `cosmetic-both-procedures-unmet`, and it is the only
//   case in the suite that proves the hoist. When a disposition oracle cannot see a re-route, the
//   defence is a case whose ROUTE differs, not a case whose answer differs.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
decision "Blepharoplasty And Blepharoptosis Repair Coverage Determination":
first:
- when ( "Blepharoplasty Requested" or "Blepharoptosis Repair Requested" ) then:
    first:
    - when "Performed For Cosmetic Purposes" then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
    - when ( "Blepharoplasty Requested" and "Blepharoptosis Repair Requested" ) then:
        first:
        - when ( "Qualifying Functional Indication" and "Qualifying Patient Complaint Documented" and "Qualifying Objective Demonstration Submitted" and "The Requested Blepharoplasty Is Individually Documented" and "The Requested Blepharoptosis Repair Is Individually Documented" ) then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."certify.Met".
        - otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
        end.
    - when ( "Qualifying Functional Indication" and "Qualifying Patient Complaint Documented" and "Qualifying Objective Demonstration Submitted" ) then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."certify.Met".
    - otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
    end.
- otherwise then recommend activity "Medical Policy Determination"."not-certify.Unmet".
